# LSDV Genomics Pipeline

A comprehensive bioinformatics pipeline for analyzing Lumpy Skin Disease Virus (LSDV) sequencing data using graph genomics approaches.

## Overview

This pipeline processes LSDV sequencing data through quality control, graph-based read mapping, and multi-method variant calling. It supports analysis against reference genomes of varying complexity (1, 3, 6, or 121 genomes) and provides comprehensive variant calling using three different methodologies.

## Features

- **Graph-based genomics**: Uses `vg` toolkit for graph genome construction and mapping
- **Multi-reference support**: Handles 1, 3, 6, or 121-genome reference sets
- **Triple variant calling**: Implements vg, FreeBayes, and BCFtools variant callers
- **Comprehensive QC**: Quality assessment with FastQC, Qualimap, and coverage analysis
- **SLURM integration**: Designed for high-performance computing environments
- **Flexible input**: Supports both paired-end and single-end sequencing data

## Pipeline Workflow

```
[0] Graph Genome Indexing (one-time setup)
     ↓
[1] Quality Control & Trimming
     ↓
[2] Graph-based Read Mapping (vg giraffe)
     ↓
[3] BAM Processing & Quality Assessment
     ↓
[4] Variant Calling - vg (graph-based)
     ↓
[5] Variant Calling - FreeBayes
     ↓
[6] Variant Calling - BCFtools
     ↓
[7] Variant Statistics & Comparison
     ↓
[8] Consensus Sequence Generation
```

## Requirements

### Software Dependencies

